---
source: crates/dreamd-cli/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: "subcommand_help(\"score\")"
---
List the top-N stored memories by salience, without a search query.

With no query every document gets a BM25 score of 1, so each row shows `bm25 ≈ 1` and `score ≈ salience`.

Usage: score [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -n, --n <N>
          Max results
          
          [default: 100]

      --explain
          Print per-hit salience factor breakdown (same blocks as `dreamd recall --explain`)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
